{"type":"text","timestamp":1794340974624,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c70e7008001WpOqPMFUYJemXt","messageID":"msg_1c70e5ee7001uZ0dPltS4pAvFN","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"text","text":"<think>The lock file has hashes for some but pip requires all. Let me install without the constraints but with pinned versions from requirements.txt, and separately with hashes mode disabled: `pip install --no-deps`? Simpler: install each package individually with `--no-build-isolation`? The error is due to require-hashes auto-enabled because lock has hashes for some packages but not all. Let me just install requirements.txt directly (pins present).\n\nAlso note the Docker build uses `-r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` which will hit the same hash error! Wait — in Docker, pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock: the constraints file has hashes, which triggers require-hashes mode for all packages... Actually pip's require-hashes mode is triggered by hashes in the requirements file, and constraints with hashes... Let me check: pip docs say if any hash is present in a requirements file, hash-checking mode is enabled for that file. Constraints files with hashes also trigger it. The Docker build might fail! That's a pre-existing scaffold issue — but the task says the app is built from the Dockerfile, so the build must succeed. Let me examine requirements.lock content more closely.\n\nActually the error says \"Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements\". Since some entries in the lock have hashes and others don't, pip enables hash mode and fails. Let me look at the lock file.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794340974600,"end":1794340974620}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794340974650,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-f0007378-3543-4755-8686-12673188dcf4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n -B3 -A12 \"^[a-z]\" /workspace/backend/requirements.lock | head -80"},"output":"1:blinker==1.9.0 \\\n2-    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n3-    --hash=sha256:ba0efaa9080b619ff2f3459d1d500c57bddea4a6b424b60a91141db6fd2f08bc\n4-    # via flask\n5:click==8.5.0 \\\n6-    --hash=sha256:255bc9599cf7748b4b1a446ccc735421bd08a2ae529a8b88597d3de5664ee360 \\\n7-    --hash=sha256:ba0d2089de75ea0310e2dde03160e6ca10009947fb95a182f9b54021bb272e34\n8-    # via flask\n9:flask==3.1.3 \\\n10-    --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94047b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb \\\n11-    --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n12-    # via -r requirements.txt\n13:gunicorn==26.2.0 \\\n14-    --hash=sha256:62b864895d9ebff0b2f9867ba04fe811c93121596540830c9c916d0769668447 \\\n15-    --hash=sha256:bd249d0b3f7972f7432f0a6b6ff3b3ee2d129f70cd1ff6c09a9dd9e29a2b88e3\n16-    # via -r requirements.txt\n17:itsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\n18-    --hash=sha256:c6242fc49e35958c8b15141343aa660db5fc54d4f13a1db01a3f5891b98700ef \\\n19-    --hash=sha256:e0050c0b7da1eea53ffaf149c0cfbb5c6e2e2b69c4bef22c81fa6eb73e5f6173\n20-    # via flask\n21:jinja2==3.1.6 \\\n22-    --hash=sha256:0137fb05990d35f1275a587e9aee6d56da821fc83491a0fb838183be43f66d6d \\\n23-    --hash=sha256:85ece4451f492d0c13c5dd7c13a64681a86afae63a5f347908daf103ce6d2f67\n24-    # via flask\n25:markupsafe==3.0.4 \\\n26-    --hash=sha256:007e1ffd9bf65bb6ee96df7b258fc632a4868dd5566037986c64781f35a36e98 \\\n27-    --hash=sha256:02fa4acbc6a3fc5c693c34d4dd8c1130b7fe99cc915181b0ddd6f72aeb296002 \\\n28-    --hash=sha256:03470d1a8268e692ecf79ecd565593e59d44219377a7ead61f1f1b94c1f7ff6b \\\n29-    --hash=sha256:04e7902ba80ee4bac1d50a549606527a