{"type":"text","timestamp":1794341014513,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c70f0bdf001ggZI8bCtN6iIEb","messageID":"msg_1c70effa3001L2a9TT4R0RuTBS","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"text","text":"<think>No docker. /tmp/opencode is allowed though the earlier error was Permission denied for mkdir /tmp/opencode/piptest — the directory exists but isn't writable? Let me check. Actually the venv creation at /tmp/opencode/venvtest may have worked. Let's check.\n\nBetter: create venv inside /workspace (gitignored?) Let me check .gitignore. There is no .gitignore in the workspace root listing. I should add one maybe, or place venv in /workspace/backend/.venv which is covered by .dockerignore `**/.venv`. Good.\n\nLet me test pip install without hashes first: pip install -r requirements.txt (no constraints) to see if network works.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794341014495,"end":1794341014510}}}
