{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794341206691,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c711fa82001IMH09TOC52l0lB","messageID":"msg_1c711d4e0001oCMAMxfWaufWSO","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794341206691,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c711fa85001fHWAS8CFh1JDkU","messageID":"msg_1c711d4e0001oCMAMxfWaufWSO","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"text","text":"<think>Good — installing directly from the lock file works (all packages have hashes). The issue was mixing `-r requirements.txt` (no hashes) with `-c requirements.lock` (with hashes) which triggers require-hashes mode. In the Docker build, the command is:\n\n```\npip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n```\n\nThat will fail the same way! Let me verify: pip enables require-hashes mode when hashes are present in a constraints file? Actually the error said \"Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode\" for flask==3.1.3, which came from requirements.txt lacking hashes while the constraints file had them. Hmm, actually pip's behavior: if any requirement (including from constraints?) has hashes... Actually pip enables hash-checking mode when *all* requirements have hashes... Let me check: pip requires that if a requirements file contains hashes, then all requirements must have hashes. With constraints providing hashes, pip may treat it as requiring hashes.\n\nThe error listed flask==3.1.3 missing hashes — flask is in requirements.txt without hashes but appears in the lock with hashes. So pip's constraints-with-hashes triggers hash checking mode.\n\nThis means the Docker build as-is would fail! Let me test that exact command in a fresh venv.\n\nActually wait — the sandbox pip may differ from Docker pip. Docker image python:3.13-slim has pip ~25.x probably similar. Let me test the exact Dockerfile command here to see.\n\nIf it fails, I need to fix the Dockerfile or the requirements files. The README says \"backend/requirements.lock holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file\". The task says the app is built from the Dockerfile in the workspace root — so the build must work. Let me test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794341206661,"end":1794341206687}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794341210197,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-b8585604-f440-4412-866c-3f037fe22b14","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3.13 -m venv /workspace/backend/.venv_docker && /workspace/backend/.venv_docker/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -8","timeout":300000},"output":"Collecting flask==3.1.3 (from -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt (line 1))\n  Downloading flask-3.1.3-py3-none-any.whl (103 kB)\nERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n","metadata":{"output":"Collecting flask==3.1.3 (from -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt (line 1))\n  Downloading flask-3.1.3-py3-none-any.whl (103 kB)\nERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3.13 -m venv /workspace/backend/.venv_docker && /workspace/backend/.venv_docker/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -8","time":{"start":179434120667