{"type":"text","timestamp":1794341219046,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c7122ad4001dYM9jZDXR2R4xs","messageID":"msg_1c712084f001rXIL6cWqrlwi0V","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"text","text":"<think>The Dockerfile's pip command fails because the constraints file has hashes which triggers require-hashes mode. This is a pre-existing issue in the scaffold: `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` — since requirements.lock contains hashes, pip switches to require-hashes mode and the requirements.txt entries lack hashes.\n\nWait, actually pip only enables require-hashes if hashes are present in a *requirements file* (-r), not constraints (-c)? The error indicates it did trigger. Hmm, in newer pip versions, constraints with hashes trigger hash checking mode? The error says \"it turns on automatically when any package has a hash\". So yes — the Docker build would fail.\n\nI need to fix this so the Docker image builds. Options:\n1. Make requirements.lock without hashes (just pinned versions) — simplest, and the README says \"backend/requirements.lock holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file.\"\n2. Add hashes to requirements.txt too.\n\nOption 1 is cleanest: keep the lock as a constraints file with pinned versions but no hash lines. But hashes give supply-chain security. Alternative: put hashes in requirements.txt as well. But then requirements.txt must list all direct deps with hashes, and the constraints file provides transitive deps... in require-hashes mode, ALL packages need hashes, and constraints entries have hashes for all of them — so requirements.txt lines need hashes too.\n\nLet me test: if requirements.txt has hashes for flask and gunicorn, and the lock provides hashes for transitive deps, does pip in require-hashes mode succeed? The constraints provide hashes for the transitives, so it should work. Let me test that.\n\nActually simpler and robust: keep requirements.txt with hashes, and lock file as is. Let me verify.\n\nBut also note that the image build requires network access to PyPI — the sandbox can install from public registries via read-only cache. Docker isn't available in the sandbox anyway, so I can't test the build. But I should make the Docker build work correctly.\n\nLet me test the hash approach in a venv.</think>\n\nThe scaffold's Docker pip command fails (`-r requirements.txt` + hashed constraints triggers `--require-hashes`). Let me verify a fix: adding hashes to `requirements.txt`.","time":{"start":1794341219028,"end":1794341219043}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794341224693,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-00b8c4f9-0ae9-4cfd-b884-3840f4e03bcb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3.13 -m venv /workspace/backend/.venv_hash2 && printf 'flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94037b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\\ngunicorn==26.2.0 --hash=sha256:62b864895d9ebff0b2f9867ba04fe811c93121596540830c9c916d0769668447 --hash=sha256:bd249d0b3f7972f7430f0a6b6ff3b3ee2d129f70cd1ff6c09a9dd9e29a2b88e3\\n' > /tmp/req_test.txt && /workspace/backend/.venv_hash2/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir -r /tmp/req_test.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -6","timeout":300000},"output":"  Getting requirements to build wheel: finished with status 'done'\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml): started\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml): finished with status 'done'\nCollecting blinker>=1.9.0 (from flask==3.1.3->-r /tmp/req_test.txt (line 1))\nERROR: In --require-hashes mode, all requirements must have their versions pinned with ==. These do not:\n    blinker>=1.9.0 from https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/10/cb/f2ad4230dc2eb1a74edf38f1a38b9b52277f75bef262d8908e60d957e13c/blinker-1.9.0-py3-none-any.whl (from flask==3.1.3->-r /tmp/req_test.txt (line 1))\n","metadata":{"output":"  Getting requirements to build wheel: finished with status 'done'\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml): started\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml): finished with status 'done'\nCollecting blinker>=1.9.0 (from flask==3.1.3->-r /tmp/req_test.txt (line 1))\nERROR: In --require-hashes mode, all requirements must have their versions pinned with ==. These do not:\n    blinker>=1.9.0 from https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/10/cb/f2ad4230dc2eb1a74edf38f1a38b9b52277f75bef262d8908e60d957e13c/blinker-1.9.0-py3-none-any.whl (from flask==3.1.3->-r /tmp/req_test.txt (line 1))\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3.13 -m venv /workspace/backend/.venv_hash2 && printf 'flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94037b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\\ngunicorn==26.2.0 --hash=sha256:62b864895d9ebff0b2f9867ba04fe811c93121596540830c9c916d0769668447 --hash=sha256:bd249d0b3f7972f7430f0a6b6ff3b3ee2d129f70cd1ff6c09a9dd9e29a2b88e3\\n' > /tmp/req_test.txt && /workspace/backend/.venv_hash2/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir -r /tmp/req_test.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -6","time":{"start":1794341219036,"end":1794341224667}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7122ad70017nc2o4O45nUP2W","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","messageID":"msg_1c712084f001rXIL6cWqrlwi0V"}}
