{"type":"text","timestamp":1794341376606,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c714924d0017vE7hHmFSAbgzY","messageID":"msg_1c7147847001vh7Rbc4w4SOojV","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"text","text":"<think>Also, the pagination helper returns a weird union type. Let me refactor it to be cleaner: return a tuple (page, page_size) or raise a custom error. Let me restructure using a small class or just return tuple and handle error separately.\n\nLet me rewrite parse_pagination to return `tuple[int, int] | tuple[Response, int]`, but the check `isinstance(pagination[1], int)` is hacky. Better: make a helper that raises a ValidationError and catch it.\n\nLet me refactor for clarity.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794341376589,"end":1794341376604}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794341376632,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-2d2eb530-d816-4e61-893b-31f657e203ac","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","newString":"def parse_pagination() -> tuple[int, int]:\n    raw_page = request.args.get(\"page\", \"1\")\n    raw_page_size = request.args.get(\"page_size\", str(DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE))\n    try:\n        page = int(raw_page)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ApiError(\"'page' must be an integer.\", 400)\n    try:\n        page_size = int(raw_page_size)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ApiError(\"'page_size' must be an integer.\", 400)\n    if page < 1:\n        raise ApiError(\"'page' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n    if page_size < 1:\n        raise ApiError(\"'page_size' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n    return page, min(page_size, MAX_PAGE_SIZE)","oldString":"def parse_pagination() -> tuple[int, int] | tuple[Response, int]:\n    raw_page = request.args.get(\"page\", \"1\")\n    raw_page_size = request.args.get(\"page_size\", str(DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE))\n    try:\n        page = int(raw_page)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return error(\"'page' must be an integer.\", 400)\n    try:\n        page_size = int(raw_page_size)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return error(\"'page_size' must be an integer.\", 400)\n    if page < 1:\n        return error(\"'page' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n    if page_size < 1:\n        return error(\"'page_size' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n    return page, min(page_size, MAX_PAGE_SIZE)","replaceAll":false},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -194,23 +194,23 @@\n         (image_id,),\n     ).fetchone()\n \n \n-def parse_pagination() -> tuple[int, int] | tuple[Response, int]:\n+def parse_pagination() -> tuple[int, int]:\n     raw_page = request.args.get(\"page\", \"1\")\n     raw_page_size = request.args.get(\"page_size\", str(DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE))\n     try:\n         page = int(raw_page)\n     except (TypeError, ValueError):\n-        return error(\"'page' must be an integer.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page' must be an integer.\", 400)\n     try:\n         page_size = int(raw_page_size)\n     except (TypeError, ValueError):\n-        return error(\"'page_size' must be an integer.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page_size' must be an integer.\", 400)\n     if page < 1:\n-        return error(\"'page' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n     if page_size < 1:\n-        return error(\"'page_size' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page_size' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n     return page, min(page_size, MAX_PAGE_SIZE)\n \n \n def create_app() -> Flask:\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/app.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -194,23 +194,23 @@\n         (image_id,),\n     ).fetchone()\n \n \n-def parse_pagination() -> tuple[int, int] | tuple[Response, int]:\n+def parse_pagination() -> tuple[int, int]:\n     raw_page = request.args.get(\"page\", \"1\")\n     raw_page_size = request.args.get(\"page_size\", str(DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE))\n     try:\n         page = int(raw_page)\n     except (TypeError, ValueError):\n-        return error(\"'page' must be an integer.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page' must be an integer.\", 400)\n     try:\n         page_size = int(raw_page_size)\n     except (TypeError, ValueError):\n-        return error(\"'page_size' must be an integer.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page_size' must be an integer.\", 400)\n     if page < 1:\n-        return error(\"'page' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n     if page_size < 1:\n-        return error(\"'page_size' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n+        raise ApiError(\"'page_size' must be 1 or greater.\", 400)\n     return page, min(page_size, MAX_PAGE_SIZE)\n \n \n def create_app() -> Flask:\n","additions":5,"deletions":5},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794341376600,"end":1794341376614}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7149252001sUo98yB4vjswHm","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","messageID":"msg_1c7147847001vh7Rbc4w4SOojV"}}
