{"type":"text","timestamp":1794341625677,"sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","part":{"id":"prt_1c7185f3d001diSInEVjSOq9eX","messageID":"msg_1c71843180015L63x1giUM1hgq","sessionID":"ses_e38f2e3bfffecd83FRQMpSQm98","type":"text","text":"<think>The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` which requires the lock file to be in sync — it is now since npm install updated package-lock.json. But note the caret ranges. Let me pin exact versions to match the style of the repo (react is pinned \"19.3.1\"). I'll pin exact versions and re-run npm install to update the lock.\n\nAlso, note the Docker build copies `frontend/package.json frontend/package-lock.json*` then `npm ci`. That works if lock is in sync.\n\nLet me pin the versions exactly.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794341625661,"end":1794341625673}}}
